# An outbound request, and the three states it can be in.
#
# `request` writes the host it talks to on its own line, so what this
# program fetches is decidable by reading it. What comes back is
# `Remote of Text` — the same type a `server` signal has when a browser
# reads it — so it is spent with the same three-armed `when`.
#
# The arguments become the query string, which is why they are where the
# information-flow pass rules on a request: `topic` is part of the URL.

request quote is client
    from  "/quote.txt"
    with  topic is subject
    gives Text

state subject is client Text starting "signals"

view title is "A quote"
    Column
        Heading "Ask for a quote"
        Input subject, hint is "a topic"
        when quote
            Loading show Text "asking…"
            Failed with error show Text error.message
            Ready with body
                Text body
